Australian place directory (au_cities.csv)

Derived from GeoNames (https://www.geonames.org/), licensed under the
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0):
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Obtained through the npm package "all-the-cities" version 3.1.0 (MIT licence
for the package code; the package states that its data is derived from
GeoNames). The raw package tarball is not committed. Only the Australian rows
were extracted by tools/extract_all_the_cities.py into au_cities.csv.

Selection: country AU with population >= 15,000, plus the eight state and
territory capitals. Coordinates are rounded to four decimals. The timezone
column is a hand-assigned IANA zone per state (Broken Hill is the only
city-level exception). The state column uses GeoNames admin1 codes 01-08.

This is a weather and display directory, not a postal or administrative
register.
